 orquestales anticipan el trip-hop; Van Dyke Parks y su música de cámara pop; David Ackles, Kim Fowley, Wild Man Fischer) y los herederos del Greenwich (Laura Nyro, Eric Andersen, David Peel, Angus MacLise y Nico, cuyas letanías fúnebres inventan el rock gótico casi por accidente: Marble Index, Desert Shore). Canadá aporta a Leonard Cohen, Gordon Lightfoot, Joni Mitchell (Blue, Hejira) y Neil Young, que con Dylan y Springsteen forma la gran tríada «moral» de la música americana e inventa la guitarra distorsionada que influirá en el grunge. En Texas, Townes Van Zandt; en Gran Bretaña, Scott Walker, Nick Drake (Pink Moon), Roy Harper, John Martyn, Cat Stevens, Rod Stewart, Eric Burdon y Jack Bruce.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":141040069985257,"artist":"Laura Nyro","artist_id":50489031009532,"title":"More Than a New Discovery","year":1966,"ess":1,"yt":"HimC7RmLhm0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","scene_id":243962098886055,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s","chapters":["Sección 3.3"],"pages":[[1,51,null]]},{"id":37859659373048,"artist":"Laura Nyro","artist_id":50489031009532,"title":"Eli And The Thirteenth Confession","year":1968,"ess":0,"yt":"_kPrm5uHz0Y","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","scene_id":243962098886055,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s","chapters":["Sección 3.3"],"pages":[[1,51,null]]},{"id":223426625176223,"artist":"Laura Nyro","artist_id":50489031009532,"title":"New York Tendaberry","year":1969,"ess":1,"yt":"t3C63fS3Dqo","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","scene_id":243962098886055,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s","chapters":["Sección 3.3"],"pages":[[1,51,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":36,"text":"• Nihilist Spasm Band: No Record (Allied Record Corporation, 1968) • Laura Nyro: More Than A New Discovery (Verve, 1966) • Laura Nyro: New York Tendaberry (1969) • VanDyke Parks: Song Cycle (WB, 1968) • Pearls Before Swine: One Nation Underground (ESP, 1967) • Pentangle:…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":51,"text":"…grooves in the history of music, Spirit In The Sky (1969). Post-Greenwich 1967-71 One of the most erudite and sensitive songwriters of all times, Laura Nyro (3) devoted her career to intimate, introverted, self-analyzing songs. Her intense, intricate phrasing was the sonic equivalent of a psychoanalytic session, testing the deep, deep recesses of her psyche. Nyro embodied both the city's musical melting-pot (folk, gospel, soul, blues, jazz, musical, classical) and the city's neuroses and alienation. Nyro's…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":51,"text":"…gospel-soul constructions. New York Tendaberry (1969) was less intense but more musical. Of all the vestals to parade on the stage of pop music, Nyro remains the most awe-inspiring. Arlo Guthrie was briefly popular for the colloquial rant Alice's Restaurant (1967), that mixed Woody Allen comedy…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":252,"text":"…suffocating What Would The Community Think (1996). The latter formulated an art that took the shy pessimism of auteurs such as Nick Drake and Laura Nyro to a new dimension of introspection. Its sketchy vignettes and self-analyses coined a subtle and almost embarrassing format, that turned the…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":315,"text":"…is founded in London ？ Robert Moog begins selling his synthesizer ？ Other significant albums of the year: 13th Floor Elevator's Psychedelic Sound, Laura Nyro's More Than A New Discovery, Fugs' Second Album, West Coast Pop Art Experimental Band's Part One ？ A \"Human Be-In\" is held at the Golden Gate Park…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":328,"text":"…to compose music ？ Elton John's Candle in the Wind becomes the best-selling song of all times, passing Bing Crosby's White Christmas 1997 ？ Laura Nyro dies ？ Tim Taylor of Brainiac dies ？ John Denver dies ？ The Terrastock festival for psychedelic music is held in Providence (Rhode Island) 328"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":141040069985257,"type":"album","name":"More Than A New Discovery","list_id":73476221503278,"list":"RYM Top — Jazz — Vocal Jazz","src":"musthear","rank":46,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"q_qMp7U6gfk","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":141040069985257,"type":"album","name":"More Than A New Discovery","list_id":106824060559178,"list":"RYM Top — R&B — Pop Soul","src":"musthear","rank":19,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"q_qMp7U6gfk","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":141040069985257,"type":"album","name":"More Than A New Discovery","list_id":202254272888124,"list":"RYM Top — R&B — Soul","src":"musthear","rank":172,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"q_qMp7U6gfk","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":141040069985257,"type":"album","name":"More Than A New Discovery","work_year":1967,"list_id":170088453171885,"list":"Scaruffi 1960s","src":"charts","rank":157,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"q_qMp7U6gfk","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":37859659373048,"type":"album","name":"Eli and the Thirteenth Confession","work_year":1968,"list_id":192934750972716,"list":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","src":"charts","rank":11